This repository holds work under two licences.

GPL-2.0 (the full text is in kernel/COPYING):
  kernel/5.4/audio_driver/      Unisoc's GPL-2.0 audio driver sources for the 5.4 kernel, as published in realme's
                                kernel source release (https://github.com/realme-kernel-opensource/
                                realme_C51_C53_Narzo-N53-AndroidT-kernel-source, kernel_modules/kernel5.4/audio_driver,
                                revision 4381465ccaf87fcf3215b9cd42f4a685df40e5e0; kernel/5.4/SOURCE), unchanged
  kernel/5.4/patches/           patches to them
  kernel/mainline/sprd_audio/   the same drivers ported to the mainline kernels (from mu300-linux's
                                upstream/modules/sprd_audio), with the vendor AGCP DMA driver of Enceka/linux-lts-e5
  the drivers built from them   (modules/ in the release tarballs), and the build kits of the kernels they are built
                                against (the kits-* releases: Linux's and the vendor kernel's own headers and build files)

MIT (below): everything else - install.sh, uninstall.sh, lib/, device/, hooks/, kernel/*.sh and kernel/kits/,
src/, tools/, tests/, .github/.

Not covered by either, and not in this repository or any of its releases: the AGDSP firmware and the vendor
parameter files, which belong to Unisoc / ZTE. The firmware is fetched on the device at install time (from
github.com/dikeckaan/mu300-audio-firmware, used only with its pinned sha256), or you supply your own.

